 "text": "Good day. What's going on? No problem. What's up? Yeah, that's a good question. I think people split costs in different ways. Some people take turns paying, or they all pitch in a set amount. That's strange. Is it written in their contract, or are they just offering? No, not at all. It' just how things happen. Sometimes, families just work things out without a formal agreement. If you want to discuss with your parents, that's good. If they say no, it's up to you to figure it out. That's a good idea. Let them both talk and see what they decide. It's okay. You can ask them to talk it out.",
